// singular and plural existential binders
let m, n be odd integers.
then exists k in integers st m = 2k + 1.
there are l in integers such that n = 2l + 1.
there is integers a, b such that m = 2a + 1 and n = 2b + 1.
there exist j in N with j > n.
there are no integer x such that x^2 = 2.
therefore m + n = 2(a + b + 1) is even.
